**How to implement.** refractiveindex.info's two file kinds are read by one module (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy': a second parser for one format is a defect): the importer already reads a record page (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:RefractiveIndexInfoText.importMaterial`, tabulated `nk` and formula 1-7 pages, a tabulated page through step 2's `TabulatedNK` table), and it gains the database's catalog and a page's references (001 §D 'The existing YAML importer (`MaterialImport`) is REUSED as the record parser'; the S13.1 brief: search runs over the snapshot's catalog). The layout is the database's (`polyanskiy/refractiveindex.info-database`, branch `main`): `database/catalog-nk.yml` is a YAML list of `SHELF` items, each with a `name` and a `content` list of `DIVIDER` and `BOOK` items; a `BOOK` has a `name` and a `content` list of `DIVIDER` and `PAGE` items; a `PAGE` has a `name` and a `data` path relative to `database/data/` (for example `main/Ag/nk/Johnson.yml`). A page opens with `REFERENCES:` and `COMMENTS:` before its `DATA:` list. No YAML package is added; the reading stays line-based, as the page reading is. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.1. In `MaterialImport.fs`, which now also opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles` and `OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialSources`: (1) `ImportError` gains `member this.describe : string`: `MalformedYamlErr r` renders `the page is malformed: <r>`, `MalformedCsvErr r` `the CSV is malformed: <r>`, `NoDataErr r` `the file holds no data: <r>` and `UnsupportedFormulaErr (n, r)` `formula <n> is not supported: <r>`, so an import error renders through its own member (ELEV002). (2) `RefractiveIndexInfoCatalogText of string` with `.value`, the text of a database's `catalog-nk.yml`. `type RefractiveIndexInfoCatalogText with member this.hits : Result<MaterialSourceHit list, ImportError>` (step 443's `MaterialSourceHit`) reads it line by line, skipping a line whose trimmed text starts with `#`: `- SHELF:`, `- BOOK:` and `- PAGE:` open a shelf, a book (its page closed) and a page, keyed by the text after the colon; `name:` names the item opened last; `data:` gives the open page its record; `- DIVIDER:`, `content:` and any other key are skipped. A value has its surrounding white space and one pair of enclosing `"` or `'` removed. Each page with a `data:` is one hit, in catalog order: `record = MaterialSourceRecordId <the data text>` and `name = EntryName "<book name>, <page name>"`, an item without `name:` taking its key. A catalog listing no page is `NoDataErr`, and every .NET call that throws is caught and answered `MalformedYamlErr`. (3) `type RefractiveIndexInfoText with member this.referencesOpt : EntryCitation option` reads the page's `REFERENCES:` line: a value other than `|` is the citation, unquoted as in (2); `|` takes the following lines indented deeper than the key, each trimmed, the non-empty ones joined by one space; a page without the key, or with an empty value, answers `None`. No HTML or Markdown is stripped. `importMaterial` is unchanged: its tabulated and formula readings are where a pulled record's physics comes from. (4) Fixture: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/fixtures/catalog-nk.yml`, a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `fixtures/Si.yml`'s with no comment, holding the database's three header comment lines (`# this file is part of refractiveindex.info database`, `# refractiveindex.info database is in the public domain`, `# copyright and related rights waived via CC0 1.0`), a top-level `DIVIDER`, and two shelves: `main` named `MAIN - simple inorganic materials`, holding a `DIVIDER` and the book `Si` named `Si (Silicon)` whose page `Test` is named `Test 2026: n,k 0.25–0.70 µm` with `data: main/Si/nk/Test.yml`; and `glass` named `GLASS - optical glass`, holding the book `BK7` named `BK7 (test)` whose page `Test` is named `Test 2026: n 0.3–2.5 µm` with `data: glass/test/BK7/nk/Test.yml`. Every name is double-quoted. (5) Tests, in `MaterialImportTests`: `the refractiveindex.info catalog lists each page as a hit named by its book and page`: `(RefractiveIndexInfoCatalogText <fixtures/catalog-nk.yml>).hits` answers exactly `main/Si/nk/Test.yml` named `Si (Silicon), Test 2026: n,k 0.25–0.70 µm` and `glass/test/BK7/nk/Test.yml` named `BK7 (test), Test 2026: n 0.3–2.5 µm`, in that order; a test-local catalog whose page has no `name:` names it by its key; and a catalog of header comments alone answers `NoDataErr`. `a page's references are its citation, a block's lines joined`: `fixtures/Si.yml` answers its quoted `REFERENCES` text unquoted; a test-local page whose `REFERENCES: |` block spans three indented lines answers them joined by single spaces; and a page without the key answers `None`. `every import error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason, `UnsupportedFormulaErr` of formula 8, renders a distinct text holding it.

**Acceptance.** After the readers land, `MaterialImport` MUST read a refractiveindex.info catalog into `MaterialSourceHit`s and a page's references into a citation, and `ImportError` MUST render through `describe`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the refractiveindex.info catalog lists each page as a hit named by its book and page`, `a page's references are its citation, a block's lines joined` and `every import error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 3; kit-acceptance MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests with AT-1 and AT-2 expectations and tolerances unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s43 invariants MUST pass.
